WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:04.830
Donald Trump has commuted the sentence of
his campaign associate, Roger Stone.

00:00:04.830 --> 00:00:08.890
Roger Stone, therefore, will not be going
to prison where he was scheduled to report

00:00:08.890 --> 00:00:09.890
soon.

00:00:09.890 --> 00:00:13.980
Now, there's the general discussion here and
then there's the specific discussion.

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:19.170
And I think it makes sense to go in that order
in general when presidents pardon people or

00:00:19.170 --> 00:00:21.210
commute their sentences.

00:00:21.210 --> 00:00:27.170
It's very common that red flags come up about
connections between the presidents and the

00:00:27.170 --> 00:00:31.500
people they are pardoning or whose sentences
they're commuting.

00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:37.469
Were they friends or whatever the case may
be in this case? Trump is commuting the sentence

00:00:37.469 --> 00:00:38.980
not just of a friend.

00:00:38.980 --> 00:00:45.379
To the extent that Donald Trump has friendships,
but of a friend who worked to get Donald Trump

00:00:45.379 --> 00:00:46.739
elected.

00:00:46.739 --> 00:00:48.839
But it isn't just that.

00:00:48.839 --> 00:00:57.280
It's a friend whose crime was directly related
to helping to get Donald Trump elected.

00:00:57.280 --> 00:01:04.629
But it's even more the reason that Roger Stone
lied in relation to his work.

00:01:04.629 --> 00:01:11.369
Getting Donald Trump elected was to protect
Trump by hiding wrongdoing that Donald Trump

00:01:11.369 --> 00:01:17.840
may have been involved in and incomes Donald
Trump and Commute's Roger Stone's sentence.

00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:23.640
This is exactly as Republican Senator Mitt
Romney, of all people, said, it is historic

00:01:23.640 --> 00:01:25.110
corruption.

00:01:25.110 --> 00:01:29.869
Roger Stone was a GO-BETWEEN for the Trump
campaign and WikiLeaks.

00:01:29.869 --> 00:01:34.200
Roger Stone was materially involved in the
Trump campaign.

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:41.790
Roger Stone was convicted by a jury for lying
to Congress to protect Donald Trump.

00:01:41.790 --> 00:01:45.380
So this is corruption.

00:01:45.380 --> 00:01:47.600
This is an abuse of power.

00:01:47.600 --> 00:01:49.460
This is a quid pro quo.

00:01:49.460 --> 00:01:55.840
Remember that phrase that Trump threw around
to stay strong when it was Paul Manafort and

00:01:55.840 --> 00:01:57.560
Michael Cohen?

00:01:57.560 --> 00:02:02.210
Trump's former campaign chairman and former
personal lawyer who were under investigation

00:02:02.210 --> 00:02:06.829
and under indictment, Donald Trump tweeted
about Manafort is staying strong.

00:02:06.829 --> 00:02:09.390
What that means is he's protecting Donald
Trump.

00:02:09.390 --> 00:02:13.090
Well, Roger Stone stayed strong in that vein.

00:02:13.090 --> 00:02:14.630
He didn't roll over.

00:02:14.630 --> 00:02:18.260
He didn't talk about what Trump knew and what
Trump did.

00:02:18.260 --> 00:02:20.070
And that is a quid pro quo.

00:02:20.070 --> 00:02:22.060
This is arguably a form of bribery.

00:02:22.060 --> 00:02:24.720
This is arguably an impeachable offense.

00:02:24.720 --> 00:02:28.000
Now, Trump and others will argue, and it's
important to be prepared for this.

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:32.370
They will say the president's power to pardon
and commute sentences is absolute.

00:02:32.370 --> 00:02:38.210
Yeah, it's absolute in that a president can
pardon whoever they want to pardon or commute

00:02:38.210 --> 00:02:41.850
the sentence sentence of whoever they want
to commute a sentence for.

00:02:41.850 --> 00:02:48.380
But that doesn't mean that it can't also be
an act of corruption or a quid pro quo or

00:02:48.380 --> 00:02:49.510
a form of bribery.

00:02:49.510 --> 00:02:53.230
And only two Republicans so far have actually
called this out for what it is.

00:02:53.230 --> 00:02:59.620
One is Mitt Romney, as I mentioned, Mitt Romney
tweeted, quote, unprecedented historic corruption.

00:02:59.620 --> 00:03:06.150
An American president commutes the sentence
of a person convicted by a jury of lying to

00:03:06.150 --> 00:03:08.760
shield that very president.

00:03:08.760 --> 00:03:11.080
Now, you know, good for Mitt Romney.

00:03:11.080 --> 00:03:17.330
But remember, Romney voted to convict Trump
on one impeachment count, but he voted to

00:03:17.330 --> 00:03:19.700
acquit Donald Trump on obstruction.

00:03:19.700 --> 00:03:24.000
And now Mitt Romney is indignant that Donald
Trump is again obstructing.

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:25.000
Give me a break.

00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:26.000
So I get it.

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:28.540
Mitt Romney is saying things most Republicans
aren't willing to say.

00:03:28.540 --> 00:03:30.790
But at the same time, you acquitted the guy
on obstruction.

00:03:30.790 --> 00:03:32.000
You remember that, right?

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:37.640
Then you have Republican Senator Pat Toomey
who said that the prosecution of Roger Stone

00:03:37.640 --> 00:03:42.820
was a righteous and appropriate prosecution,
quoting William Barr had to say, and that

00:03:42.820 --> 00:03:47.180
if there was a problem with this prosecution,
it really should be resolved via an appeal,

00:03:47.180 --> 00:03:51.651
not between not by Donald Trump jumping in
and commuting the sentence of Roger Stone

00:03:51.651 --> 00:03:54.320
if Soane was treated unfairly in a real sense.

00:03:54.320 --> 00:03:59.670
But we are well within the scope of time during
which an appeal can be made and it could actually

00:03:59.670 --> 00:04:01.010
be fought through the courts.

00:04:01.010 --> 00:04:04.460
So the action by Trump here is not surprising.

00:04:04.460 --> 00:04:08.920
The realization that we've come to is that
until Republicans are forced to do what's

00:04:08.920 --> 00:04:12.730
right or stopped from doing what's wrong,
they're going to keep doing it.

00:04:12.730 --> 00:04:18.010
And we're you know, I think maybe there's
not that much I have to say about Stone specifically.

00:04:18.010 --> 00:04:21.010
I think it's basically, albeit been said.

00:04:21.010 --> 00:04:26.050
But what sometimes happens in these situations
is that some on the left will say.

00:04:26.050 --> 00:04:33.130
Saying, should we stoop to their level, like,
are they so bad that we should resort to cheating

00:04:33.130 --> 00:04:36.710
or violence or corruption in order to get
them out?

00:04:36.710 --> 00:04:40.920
Does the ends do the ends justify the means?

00:04:40.920 --> 00:04:42.230
And I don't believe so.

00:04:42.230 --> 00:04:46.510
I don't think that you can pick and choose
when to play by the rules.

00:04:46.510 --> 00:04:50.130
And obviously, it's horrible right now when
we see the degree to which they don't play

00:04:50.130 --> 00:04:51.210
by the rules.

00:04:51.210 --> 00:04:52.810
I understand saying it.

00:04:52.810 --> 00:04:57.840
We would be justified in not playing by the
rules here because we have to get them out.

00:04:57.840 --> 00:04:59.560
I think that that would be the wrong instinct.

00:04:59.560 --> 00:05:02.210
I believe the path forward should be.

00:05:02.210 --> 00:05:08.030
You've got to remove Trump in November, turned
the Senate blue, if not this November, in

00:05:08.030 --> 00:05:10.700
November of twenty twenty two.

00:05:10.700 --> 00:05:15.720
Maybe this terror of a presidency will affect
enough voters that it will sort of predispose

00:05:15.720 --> 00:05:19.240
open up the country to accept real change.

00:05:19.240 --> 00:05:25.020
If the Democratic Party gets the country back
under control, I'm no fan of the Democratic

00:05:25.020 --> 00:05:26.190
Party as an institution.

00:05:26.190 --> 00:05:30.650
But, you know, there are people who are going
to seek to blame Democrats here.

00:05:30.650 --> 00:05:37.970
In fact, I've seen some so-called populists
over the last week finding as much to criticize

00:05:37.970 --> 00:05:43.190
of Democrats in the context of the Trump fiasco
as they find to criticize about Donald Trump

00:05:43.190 --> 00:05:44.190
himself.

00:05:44.190 --> 00:05:45.190
I think they're just wrong.

00:05:45.190 --> 00:05:49.100
The truth is, Democrats, for all of their
faults and there are many and I talk about

00:05:49.100 --> 00:05:50.430
them all the time.

00:05:50.430 --> 00:05:52.430
Democrats tried to investigate Trump.

00:05:52.430 --> 00:05:55.890
They saw facts which pointed to impeachment
being the right remedy.

00:05:55.890 --> 00:05:56.890
And they did it.

00:05:56.890 --> 00:05:57.890
It didn't matter.

00:05:57.890 --> 00:05:59.370
The Republican Party was never going to go
for it.

00:05:59.370 --> 00:06:03.230
We never believed for a second that Trump
was going to be convicted on impeachment.

00:06:03.230 --> 00:06:07.410
But the Democrats saw the evidence and said
impeachment is the correct thing.

00:06:07.410 --> 00:06:12.570
Democrats were obstructed by the Trump administration
and by Republicans at every turn.

00:06:12.570 --> 00:06:16.980
So there are plenty of critiques of the Democratic
Party, and I make them all the time.

00:06:16.980 --> 00:06:21.830
But right now, deflecting blame onto the Democratic
Party is the wrong move.

00:06:21.830 --> 00:06:27.461
Right now, it's the Republican Party under
Trump ism that either participated in the

00:06:27.461 --> 00:06:31.970
attacks on the rule of law or as they stood
aside, as Trump did it himself.

00:06:31.970 --> 00:06:33.680
And they need to be held accountable as well.

00:06:33.680 --> 00:06:34.680
That's very important.

00:06:34.680 --> 00:06:38.870
They are also to blame and you primarily should
be blaming the bad actors.

00:06:38.870 --> 00:06:40.760
So I'm not going to play coy with that.

00:06:40.760 --> 00:06:46.390
The way there are some people doing New York
maybe should look at prosecuting Roger Stone.

00:06:46.390 --> 00:06:50.910
The president can't pardon or commute state
sentences and convictions.

00:06:50.910 --> 00:06:53.670
So on the stone matter, that would be something
to look at.

00:06:53.670 --> 00:06:55.603
But big picture, we really can't miss the
forest for the trees right now

